{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3276","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3276","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3276\",\"parent_revision\":\"5378b811ab204fa9e820db64ece0ca95d2385d0c\",\"root_revision\":\"1fc9dfbc859dab7833fe8c674a1a802f9858a8798761f85444deff93d1daa965\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`agents/contract-verification.md` line 151 states: \\\"Your finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there \u2014 you register no artifact and write no task state.\\\" This assumes a synchronous dispatch model where the caller receives the subagent's final text as a direct return value.\\n\\nObserved during this session while running `/dh:implement-feature` on plan Pd95e593c for #3151: dispatching `dh:contract-verification` via the `Agent` tool returned only an async \\\"Spawned successfully\\\" acknowledgment. The agent completed its analysis and went idle twice (confirmed via `ListAgents`), but no message with actual content was ever delivered back \u2014 only bare `idle_notification` events with no `summary` field, unlike every other subagent dispatched in the same session (impact-analyst, fact-checker, classifier, rtica-assessor, alignment-analyst, groomer, feature-researcher, architect, swarm-task-planner, t0/t1 task agents), all of which reported back with a `summary` field containing real content. Sending the idle agent a direct follow-up question asking it to restate its verdict also produced no reply.\\n\\nThe `Agent` tool's own documentation states: \\\"Your plain text output is NOT visible to other agents \u2014 to communicate, you MUST call [SendMessage].\\\" That is the observed cause: `contract-verification.md`'s instructions never tell the agent to call `SendMessage`; they tell it to just \\\"output\\\" its finding as its response, consistent with a synchronous dispatch model this environment does not use for agent-tool dispatch.\\n\\nImpact: `implement-feature`'s Progress Loop step 4a (post-task contract verification) silently produces no usable result under this environment's async dispatch \u2014 the orchestrator either blocks indefinitely waiting for a message that never arrives, or gives up and has to verify the contract manually (as happened this session), defeating the point of delegating the check.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: this is the same class of gap already fixed for a sibling agent \u2014 `git log` shows a merged commit \\\"fix(development-harness): add SendMessage completion report to impact-analyst (#3249)\\\" that added exactly this kind of completion-report step to `dh:impact-analyst`. `dh:contract-verification` appears to have been missed by that same fix, and other `dh:*` agents dispatched by the same Progress Loop may share the identical gap \u2014 not verified for any agent besides contract-verification in this session.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: possible directions for grooming to evaluate, not requirements \u2014 (1) add an explicit `SendMessage` step to `contract-verification.md`'s Output Format section, mirroring whatever change PR #3249 made to `impact-analyst.md`; (2) audit the other `dh:*` agents invoked by `implement-feature`/`add-new-feature`'s Progress Loop for the same synchronous-response assumption, since any could have the identical gap and it would surface the same way (silent, not an error).\\n\\n**User-provided context** (added during grooming, 2026-08-29): another possible direction for grooming/planning to evaluate, not a requirement \u2014 don't make `dh:contract-verification` (or any sibling agent with the same gap) into a `TeamCreate` teammate just to get a working report-back channel. Keep it a plain background `Agent()` spawn, but have it write its result directly to the backend (e.g. `backlog_groom` on the Concerns section, or `artifact_register`, mirroring how `dh:t0-baseline-capture` reports) instead of relying on a returned value or on `SendMessage(to=\\\"team-lead\\\")` \u2014 there is no team-lead when there is no team.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T14:41:39.625254Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: contract-verification agent's findings never reach the orchestrator under async subagent dispatch\\nDate: 2026-08-29\\nGoal: Determine why contract-verification's findings never reach the implement-feature orchestrator under async Agent() dispatch, and specify the correct fix consistent with current architecture direction.\\nConditions:\\n1. Agent() tool dispatch is asynchronous for non-fork subagents in this environment (no synchronous return of final text to the caller) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. contract-verification is dispatched via a bare `Agent()` call in implement-feature/SKILL.md step 4a, not via TeamCreate teammate pattern | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. contract-verification.md's current \\\"Your finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there\\\" line was a deliberate change in PR #3202 (`route agent handoffs through the backend, not SendMessage`), which replaced an earlier SendMessage-to-team-lead pattern \u2014 it is not an oversight from PR #3249's impact-analyst-specific fix | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Whether other dh:* agents dispatched via bare Agent() in implement-feature/add-new-feature's Progress Loop share the identical synchronous-return assumption | Status: DERIVABLE\\n5. Established backend-routing pattern for single-shot (non-team) verification agents \u2014 e.g. dh:t0-baseline-capture registers results via `artifact_register` instead of relying on a returned value \u2014 that contract-verification could adopt | Status: DERIVABLE\\n6. Whether SendMessage from a standalone (non-team) Agent()-spawned agent reaches the orchestrator's context in this environment at all, or only teammates spawned via TeamCreate can address a \\\"team-lead\\\" | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 3\\nDERIVABLE count: 3\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-28/29, while running /dh:implement-feature on plan Pd95e593c (#3151), dispatching dh:contract-verification for task T1\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"dffbc7ee75b82f6d298e6237a421f8fb0a9965249ad093c876fa90e3c5e01210\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRRUyPg\"}"}